<article class="env-lemma" id="0GKR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GKR">Lemma <span data-tag="0GKR">63.12.4</span>.</a> Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field. Let $X$ be a separated scheme of finite type type over $k$ of dimension $\leq 1$. Let $\Lambda $ be a Noetherian ring. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a constructible sheaf of $\Lambda $-modules on $X$ which is torsion. Then $H^ q_ c(X, \mathcal{F})$ is a finite $\Lambda $-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a consequence of Étale Cohomology, Theorem <a href="/tag/0GJI" data-tag="0GJI">59.84.7</a>. Namely, choose a compactification $j : X \to \overline{X}$. After replacing $\overline{X}$ by the scheme theoretic closure of $X$, we see that we may assume $\dim (\overline{X}) \leq 1$. Then $H^ q_ c(X, \mathcal{F}) = H^ q(\overline{X}, j_!\mathcal{F})$ and the theorem applies. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>